
title: Na_Start_Day2
---
Napoleon: Detective. A sigh for the sore eye.
Napoleon: *He looks drained, dark circles under his eyes. Several precarious towers of paper teeter on the table.*
    -> You: You look dreadful.
    -> You: *Gestures toward the stacks of paper* resumes?
Napoleon: *sighs* And more. The local journalists have caught wind of the murder.
Napoleon: I am attempting to persuade them to keep it under wraps. In exchange, I have granted them an exclusive—interviews, photographs, the whole act.
Napoleon:  I am also investigating their pasts. I have learned that it's always useful to have some leverage over a journalist…*pauses, then waves a hand* But yes, resumes as well.
    -> You: …Your career as a circus manager taught you that?
        Napoleon: *grins* People who join a traveling circus tend to be troublemakers. I have a reputation to uphold.
        Napoleon:  I can’t fully control my crew. The least I can do is control the press.
    -> You: How is it going?
        Napoleon: *Makes a vague gesture* Splendidly. I have quite enough on that kid with his ridiculous mustache to ensure he never writes another word in print…
        Napoleon: *stops abruptly* Oh, the trumpet penguin auditions? Not going great.
Napoleon: But enough about me and my clowns… *Pours tea from a delicate kettle, its handle shaped like a clown’s nose.*
Napoleon: Do you have any news for- ah. excuse my manners. would you like some tea?
-> You: Please, thank you. 
    Napoleon: *Napoleon slowly pours tea in a second cup, and slides it towards you*
    Napoleon: I'm out of sugar and milk. Poppet thinks I don't know that's her. *sighs* 
-> You: Not at the moment, thank you very much.
Napoleon: Very well. Now... *leans back and look at you* How close have we got to the cold hands of justice?
    <<jump NapNewsDayTwo>>

===
