===
title: Nap_Gloves
---
Napoleon: *looks at the pair of velvet glove in your hands* they indeed do. *Narrows his eyes* And they remain in dire need of repair.
You: Mr. Waddles doesn’t seem like a man who has patience for needlework.
Napoleon: Mr. Waddles never had much patience for anything that wasn’t Mr. Waddles. 
Napoleon: But I had hoped he might, at the very least, possess the good sense to annoy someone else enough to do that.
Napoleon: *Waves a hand dismissively* Return them when the case is closed, if you would be so kind. Someone will take over the cabin in due course.
Napoleon: *to himself* I should hope it is Teddy. The little thing has the eyes of a hawk.
You: You truly believe anyone would willingly enter that wagon? After what happened?
Napoleon: *Shrugs* The body is gone, and Waddles’ belongings shall follow, once your work is done. We leave these things behind when we move forward.
Napoleon: People come and go. The wagons remain. Live long enough on the road, and you learn that well enough.
Napoleon: *claps his hands* Now... What else do we have?
<<set $nap_gloves to true>>
<<jump NapNewsDayTwo>>

===
title: Nap_Monkeys
---

Napoleon: They are always interesting.
Napoleon: *leans forward slightly* But what of them now? Are they the ones we were seeking?
    -> You: they are certainly troublemakers, 
        You: But the details need not concern you.  
            Napoleon: *Curiously narrows his eyes* I am their superior, detective. If something stirs within this camp, it very much does concern me.
            -> You: They broke Mr. Waddles' trumpet...  
                You: They wanted to replace it at the night of the murder and failed, leaving behind a trail of incompetence.  
                Napoleon: *his eyebrows rise dramatically* I see.
                -> You:  But they did try, in their own misguided way. Their hearts were, at least, in the right place.  
                    You: They were only trying to protect themselves <i>and</i> one another.  
                -> You: They have broken into the crime scene. I do not believe their story.
                    You: They are hiding something and covering for each other.
                Napoleon: Indeed. They do have one another's backs. Sometimes... rather literally. It is a necessary bond when you find yourself thrust into the air, vulnerable and at the mercy of another's grip.
                Napoleon: *with a sigh* But, heavens above, why break the poor man's trumpet? 
                Napoleon: Then again... perhaps the real question is why it had not been broken sooner.
                    -> You: I can not say I understood his reasoning.
                    -> You: It was an accident. Widget simply wished to try the trumpet.  
                        Napoleon: *blinks* Widget wanted to play the trumpet?
                        Napoleon: Well, do you think he might be suitable for the position? *taps the pile of resumes, half-smiling*
                        You: Wont be less pleasant than Mr. Waddles' tunes, from what I heard.
                        Napoleon: Next we shall have Eduard performing fiery feats—jumping through rings of flame, it's time to change things around here. *muses aloud* But tell me, detective...
                        Napoleon: Are we clearing their names of suspicion?
                        -> You: I still think they are hiding something. One of them at least. That can't be the whole story.
                            Napoleon: I for one will be surprised if Widget has a secret unbeknown to Poppet.
                        -> You: They’re fools, but harmless ones, at that.  
                            Napoleon: Once, I might have said the same of all my crew. But I now know—at least one of them is far from harmless.
                    Napoleon: Well then, detective, thank you for spilling your tea. *his eyes twinkle* Is there anything more you wish to share?
                        <<set $nap_monkeyheist to true>>   
                        <<jump NapNewsDayTwo>>           
            -> You: Its most likely non related to the case.
                You: You need to ask them yourself, it's not my place to tell.
                Napoleon: *Laughs* Poppet can’t keep a secret for more than twelve hours.
                Napoleon: But I can respect one who knows how to hold their tongue. I shan't press you.
                Napoleon: So, are we removing their names from the list of suspects? Or are you merely declaring them innocence in the matter I’m yet to hear about?
                    -> You: I still think they are hiding something. One of them at least.
                        Napoleon: I’d be utterly surprised if Widget carries a secret that Poppet is unaware of.
                    -> You: They are fools. But they are harmless.
                        Napoleon: Once, I might have said the same of all my crew. But I now know—at least one of them is far from harmless.
                    Napoleon: Shame you're not spilling your tea. *his eyes twinkle* Is there anything more you wish to share?
                     <<set $nap_monkeyheist to true>>   
                    <<jump NapNewsDayTwo>> 
===
title: Nap_BrokenHearts
---
Napoleon: *Raises an eyebrow* 
You: He used to be an actor of some sort, from what I heard. Maybe he’s broken a heart or two?
Napoleon: lets his head fall back as he laughs Broken a heart or... gods.
Napoleon: I very much doubt that would be the case. Then again, what do I know.
Napoleon: I was not exactly the target audience of the man's charm.
Napoleon: Regardless, we did a quick inquiry before engaging your service. None of the locals have spotted an unfamiliar face that day.
Napoleon: As much as it pains me to admit, the killer is among us.
    -> You: I understand. Hard to believe someone you know is capable of such an act.
    -> You: I never asked—do you have suspects?
Napoleon: *is mindlessly rolling a resume* Hm? Yes, no. I can pretty much believe every single one of them capable of such an act...
    -> You: But you are not naming names.
Napoleon: *rolls a resume and taps it on the table* You might have figured out, dear detective,
Napoleon: That Waddle wasn’t exactly the most popular of the bunch.
Napoleon: I can count at least two motives for every one of them—silencing the trumpet rehearsals being the shared one.
Napoleon: *leans back* but I won’t, because I’m biased. Last thing I want is to ruin your investigation.
Napoleon: I hope it’s someone with an easy-to-refill job.
Napoleon: I wonder, by the way... how did you know about Waddle’s past career?
Napoleon: I don’t recall giving you his resume...
Napoleon: *to himself* Don’t even know where it is.
    -> You: I’m discreet about my sources.
        Napoleon: *grins* I can respect that.
        Napoleon: I also think it was Poppet. Right? Don’t answer if you don’t want to.
    -> You: Poppet seems to be quite informed about your employees.
        Napoleon: Ah, knew it.
Napoleon: *opens his arms* I do regular performance reviews with them, you see. How they’ve been doing, how it was received, how they feel...
Napoleon: Now with Poppet...
Napoleon: The tables turn. I feel like a kitten being psychoanalyzed.
You: I can imagine that. 
Napoleon: Can you now? 
<<wait 1>>
Napoleon: Aside from tracing Waddle's trail of broken heart... What else do we have to discuss?
<<set $nap_waddles_actor to true>>
<<jump NapNewsDayTwo>>
===
title: Nap_DayTwo_End
---
Napoleon: *Drumming a steady rhythm on the wooden desk with his fingernails* Please, tell me you have more.
You: I fear that is all for today.
Napoleon: *Sighs* Very well. Fortunate, then, that I planned for three days.
Napoleon: Let us hope fortune favors you more on the morrow.
Napoleon: You have the key, and you know the drill. Turn that wagon inside out—there must be something.
===
